  410\t| `dao.space.store`, `dao.stream.journal.file`,       | platform                               |                                                          |\n   411\t| `dao.data.btree.storage` (promise facade)           |                                        |                                                          |\n   412\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   413\t| 21 `random-uuid` sites in the closure (§3.2),       | Fresh entropy and identities           | External (property 3). **Deferred** (§9.1).              |\n   414\t| `rpc:114` and `jing.dht:373` `rand`,                |                                        |                                                          |\n   415\t| `space.dht/secure-random-bytes`, `sign/generate`    |                                        |                                                          |\n   416\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   417\t| `dao.jing.coordinate:80` selecting                  | JVM blocking driver with clock and     | External (property 4, 1). **Deferred** (§9.1).           |\n   418\t| `dao.jing.content.driver` (clj lane, clock, sleep,  | sleep; host promises (not timers: a    | (`dao.jing.content.async` is not in the closure, H0; its |\n   419\t| `locking`); `dao.data.btree.storage` (promise       | `CompletableFuture`/`Promise`/         | timer is out of scope until the deferred design widens   |\n   420\t| facade `:218-227`)                                  | `Completer`)                           | it.)                                                     |\n   421\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   422\t| `yin.repl.main`, `yin.repl` (`:275-277` banner),    | Clock, stdin/stdout, exit, env         | Driver. `repl.cljc:275` and `fs.cljc:271` ambient reads  |\n   423\t| `yin.repl.state` (`dart:io`, `js/require`)          |                                        | deferred (§9.1).                                         |\n   424\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   425\t| `yang.python.antlr.*`, `yang.antlr.cst` (x3),       | Generated recognizers                  | Stage: **deferred** (§9.3). (`antlr/repl.cljc:71` is a   |\n   426\t| `yang.frontend`, `yang.stage`, `yin.repl.frontends` |                                        | `println` inside a quoted yin program, the VM's own      |\n   427\t|                                                     |                                        | primitive, not a host call, V; r3's \"one `println`\" is   |\n   428\t|                                                     |                                        | withdrawn.)                                              |\n   429\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   430\t| `yang.clojure:349,359`, `yang.php:575`,             | `gensym` (process counter)             | **Deferred** (§9.1), hygiene required.                   |\n   431\t| `dao.space.transact:35`                             |                                        |                                                          |\n   432\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   433\t| `dao.data.btree` (atomic flag, weak/soft refs),     | Owned runtime state                    | Table C; no slice. (`dao.space.schema` is not in the     |\n   434\t| `locking` in `jing.file`, `journal`, `transactor`,  |                                        | closure, H0.)                                            |\n   435\t| `ucf.authority`                                     |                                        |                                                          |\n   436\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   437\t| **H0 finding, profile consumers**: byte length in   | Bytes, text, integer and float         | Internal pure: consumers of table A entries, migrated in |\n   438\t| `yin/repl/query.cljc:460`, `yin/vm/linker/          | carriers reached by hand               | H2 (`bytes/length`, `text/utf8-decode`,                  |\n   439\t| closure.cljc:32`, `yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:282`;       |                                        | `integer/parse-decimal`, `integer/safe-native?`,         |\n   440\t| `bytes->str` at `yin/vm.cljc:404`; PHP number       |                                        | `exact-integer?`/`host-float?`/`nan-float?`; the         |\n   441\t| parsing at `yang/php.cljc:95,98`; safe-integer      |                                        | portable `code-points` of `data.cljc:143-159` moves to   |\n   442\t| checks at `yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc:439`  |                                        | table B for the packet). Two **named behaviour changes** |\n   443\t| and `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:130`; the       |                                        | ride with them (§10): `bytes->str` decodes each byte as  |\n   444\t| number fast path at `dao/space/index.cljc:78`; code |                                        | a char code on JS and Dart and as UTF-8 on the JVM (V    |\n   445\t| points at `yang/antlr/packet.cljc:67`               |                                        | `vm.cljc:404-408`), and becomes strict UTF-8 on all      |\n   446\t|                                                     |                                        | three (its JVM-only encoding arity is dropped unless     |\n   447\t|                                                     |                                        | H2's audit finds a caller); `js/parseInt` at             |\n   448\t|                                                     |                                        | `php.cljc:100` loses precision above 2^53 where the JVM  |\n   449\t|                                                     |                                        | does not, and becomes exact on all three.                |\n   450\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   451\t| **H0 finding, retained dialect arms**: runtime type | A type name for diagnostics            | Dialect semantics (§2.5): display text, never persisted  |\n   452\t| name for error text at `dao/space/query.cljc:808`,  | (`.-runtimeType` on Dart, `type`       | or hashed; the EDN reader is the same function under two |\n   453\t| `yang/clojure.cljc:375`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc:929`;  | elsewhere); the dialect's EDN reader   | namespaces. Retained on list 1 under a \"dialect arms\"    |\n   454\t| the EDN reader alias at `yin/repl/adapter.cljc:58`  | (`clojure.edn` / `cljs.reader`)        | row (§8.1). No slice.                                    |\n   455\t| and `yin/repl/dht.cljc:104`                         |                                        |                                                          |\n   456\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   457\t| `dao.stream.transit`, `dao.stream.cbor`, `.codec`   | Transport codecs                       | Codec track; untouched (§8.3).                           |\n   458\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   459\t| `dao.pretty` (`pretty.cljc:8-23`, `StringWriter`,   | Formatting a value to a string; the    | Internal, pure (a string result; no world contact).      |\n   460\t| `clojure.pprint`/`cljs.pprint`, a custom cljd       | one consumer is the REPL's display     | Dialect formatting semantics: the three implementations  |\n   461\t| printer)                                            | (`repl.cljc:355`, V)                   | may format differently; the text is display only, never  |\n   462\t|                                                     |                                        | persisted or hashed. Allowlisted in list 1 (§8). No      |\n   463\t|                                                     |                                        | slice.                                                   |\n   464\t+-----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+\n   465\t\n   466\t### 3.2 Resolved effect calls, corrected (V)\n   467\t\n   468\t**Three scopes, reconciled (V, H0).** `random-uuid` occurs on **27** lines\n   469\tin `src/cljc`; **26** of them lie outside the directories OQ1 excludes (the\n   470\t27th is `dao/postgraphics/terminal.cljc:14`), which is the directory-based\n   471\treading r3 and its reviewer used; and **21** lie in the **transitive require\n   472\tclosure** from `yin.repl.main` that H0 committed, because `dao/await.cljc`\n   473\t(`:235,240`) and `yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc` (`:417,604,606`) are\n   474\trequired by no `src` file (V, H0). **The gate uses the transitive closure**:\n   475\tit is the set a running REPL composition can reach, it is committed and\n   476\tregenerated by the tool, and a file no `src` namespace requires cannot\n   477\taffect a host's behaviour until something requires it, at which point it\n   478\tenters the closure and the gate sees it. The five out-of-closure sites are\n   479\trecorded for the deferred design (§9.1) as reachable only from tests or\n   480\tnot at all. The 21: `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:27,185`; `memory_log.cljc:73`;\n   481\t`ws.cljc:122`; `remote.cljc:1249`; `remote_pair.cljc:180`;\n   482\t`remote_route.cljc:173`; `journal.cljc:296`; `dao/jing/content/step.cljc:132`;\n   483\t`dao/lease.cljc:594`; `dao/space/store/fs.cljc:137,351`;\n   484\t`yin/vm/linker.cljc:1685`; `yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc:46`;\n   485\t`yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:1507`; `yin/vm/telemetry.cljc:112`;\n   486\t`yin/repl.cljc:667,668,733,918`; `yin/repl/dht.cljc:117`.\n   487\t\n   488\tOther sources, as the H0 gate resolves them (V): `rand` at\n   489\t`rpc.cljc:114-116`, `rand-int` at `jing/dht.cljc:373`; secure generators at\n   490\t`space/dht.cljc:142-151` and `sign.cljc:119-123`, plus `sign.cljc:79`, the\n   491\tdeterministic seed-replay proxy, which matches by name and sits in list 2's\n   492\tceiling for that file with a comment (§2.5 rules it internal); `gensym` at\n   493\tthree sites; clocks at `main.cljc:1242,1275,1408,1435,1542` (driver),\n   494\t`driver.clj:169,206` (JVM lane) and the three ws seams (`ws/jvm.clj:422`,\n   495\t`ws/node.cljs:249`, `ws/dart.cljd:176`, seam-private); ambient at\n   496\t`fs.cljc:92,136,271-273`, `repl.cljc:275-277`, `main.cljc`; printing at\n   497\t`main.cljc`: **13 resolved calls** (`println`, `print`, `flush`,\n   498\t`js/console.log`; r3's \"19\" counted lines by text, including `*out*`\n   499\tmentions and docstrings, and is withdrawn); `antlr/repl.cljc:71` is not a\n   500\thost call (§3.1). Timers the gate sees: `driver.clj:173` (`Thread/sleep`),\n   501\t`datagram/jvm.clj:70` and the three waitset drivers; `storage.cljc:224-227`\n   502\tis a promise facade, not a timer, and `main.cljc:1321,1343` construct\n   503\tthreads (driver). All are deferred-scope entries (§9) or seam/driver\n   504\tsites; none is in an H0-H4 file.\n   505\t\n   506\t### 3.3 Exempt dialect syntax\n   507\t\n   508\tNot host contact; the H0 gate exempts them by pattern: `catch` type arms;\n   509\t`^long`/`^bytes`/`^String` hints; protocol and interface names in `deftype`\n   510\tbodies and `print-method`; `exists?`; `js-obj`/`(Object.)` opaque sentinels;\n   511\trequire arms whose only purpose is an alias.\n   512\t\n   513\t## 4. The host-implementation contract\n   514\t\n   515\t### 4.1 Stream implementations and their seams (external contact)\n   516\t\n   517\tUnchanged from the tree for sockets (V) and listed for completeness; the\n   518\tstorage, entropy and parser rows are deferred (§9).\n   519\t\n   520\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   521\t| Implementation             | Portable core (V)                          | Seam value a host supplies                            | Status                      |\n   522\t+============================+============================================+=======================================================+=============================+\n   523\t| Ring buffer, memory log,   | `dao.stream.ringbuffer`, `.memory_log`,    | None. (They mint identities today, §3.2: deferred.)   | Existing                    |\n   524\t| remote channel, waitset,   | `.remote_channel`, `.waitset`, `.observe`, |                                                       |                             |\n   525\t| middleware, apply          | `.middleware`, `.apply`                    |                                                       |                             |\n   526\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   527\t| WebSocket                  | `dao.stream.ws`                            | `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (`host.cljc:20-33`)     | Existing                    |\n   528\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   529\t| Datagram and UDP           | `dao.stream.datagram`, `.udp`              | `bind!` (`datagram.cljc:15-23`)                       | Existing                    |\n   530\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   531\t| Durable journal and the    | `dao.stream.journal` over `dao.jing.file`  | Deferred (§9.2)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   532\t| storage beneath it         | and `store.fs`                             |                                                       |                             |\n   533\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   534\t| Entropy                    | Deferred                                   | Deferred (§9.1)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   535\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   536\t| Parser stage               | `yang.python.antlr.*`                      | Deferred (§9.3)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   537\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   538\t| wasm import surface        | `dao.stream.wasm.md` §1                    | The seven imports                                     | Existing spec               |\n   539\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   540\t\n   541\tSeam rule (`abi.md` §6-§7 as acceptance): a seam entry is implementation-\n   542\tprivate, called only by the stream implementation that owns it; it takes\n   543\thost arguments and returns or deposits plain data; it never invokes\n   544\tapplication code; it classifies host errors into data; what it cannot do it\n   545\tanswers as a qualified unsupported outcome. A map of functions that portable\n   546\tapplication code calls to reach the world is a host service and is rejected\n   547\t(`abi.md:143-148`); none exists in H0-H4.\n   548\t\n   549\t### 4.2 The primitive profile: exact manifest (P)\n   550\t\n   551\t`dao.host.*` (OQ2 adopted) is a namespace family whose files contain only\n   552\treader-conditional entries and docstrings stating each entry's law, kind (P\n   553\tpure, M mutating per §2.4) and oracle. Table A is the profile (76 entries);\n   554\ttable B the portable code replacing host libraries; table C the runtime\n   555\tprerequisites.\n   556\t\n   557\t**Table A: profile entries.**\n   558\t\n   559\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   560\t| Namespace          | Entries (consolidated from, V)                                                                       | N   | Slice |\n   561\t+====================+======================================================================================================+=====+=======+\n   562\t| `dao.host.integer` | From `yin.vm.integer.host` (all 25, P): `big-carrier?`, `exact-integer?`, `safe-native?`,            | 28  | H1    |\n   563\t|                    | `host-float?`, `nan-float?`, `infinite-float?`, `promote`, `from-native`, `demote`, `to-native`,     |     |       |\n   564\t|                    | `native->double`, `trunc-native`, `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `quot-trunc`, `rem-trunc`, `compare-big`,     |     |       |\n   565\t|                    | `bit-and-big`, `bit-or-big`, `bit-xor-big`, `shift-left-big`, `shift-right-big`,                     |     |       |\n   566\t|                    | `magnitude-bit-length`, `to-radix-string`; from `cbor.cljc:112-254` (P): `parse-decimal` (digit      |     |       |\n   567\t|                    | string to big, refuses otherwise), `gcd`, `magnitude-bytes` (fresh bytes). `debruijn_code.cljc:315`  |     |       |\n   568\t|                    | reads `big-carrier?` (H2).                                                                           |     |       |\n   569\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   570\t| `dao.host.float`   | P: `float64->bits` (16 hex, big-endian), `bits->float64`, `finite?`, `integral?`, `fields` (sign,    | 5   | H1    |\n   571\t|                    | biased exponent, fraction big) from `cbor.cljc:525-560`, `debruijn.cljc:855-885`,                    |     |       |\n   572\t|                    | `debruijn_code.cljc:232-242` (little-endian hex becomes a portable byte reversal over                |     |       |\n   573\t|                    | `float64->bits`, H2), `data.cljc:77-92`.                                                             |     |       |\n   574\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   575\t| `dao.host.number`  | The Jing numeric carriers and their host construction and access, from `cbor.cljc:342-460,483-632`   | 10  | H1    |\n   576\t|                    | (P): `float64-of`, `float-value`, `decimal?`, `decimal-of` (exponent, mantissa; refuses outside the  |     |       |\n   577\t|                    | JVM scale window, `:552-574`), `decimal-exponent`, `decimal-mantissa`, `ratio?`, `ratio-of`          |     |       |\n   578\t|       