-----------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   592\t| `dao.host.hash`    | P: `blake3-bytes`, `sha256-bytes` (`jing.cljc:59-135`; the string forms become portable over         | 2   | H3    |\n   593\t|                    | `text`).                                                                                             |     |       |\n   594\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   595\t| `dao.host.sign`    | P: `keypair-from-seed` (`sign.cljc:75-104`, seed replay), `sign`, `verify`. `generate` (fresh        | 3   | H3    |\n   596\t|                    | entropy, `:114-124`) stays in `yin.vm.linker.sign` until the deferred design moves it.               |     |       |\n   597\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   598\t| `dao.data.arrays`  | In place (OQ2). P: `anew` (fresh), `aget`, `alength`, `aclone` (fresh), `asub` (fresh), `aconcat`    | 12  | H2    |\n   599\t| (member by         | (fresh), `ainsert-at` (fresh), `aremove-at` (fresh), `from-coll` (fresh); M: `aset`, `acopy`         |     |       |\n   600\t| reference)         | (memmove), `asort` (stable; `parallelSort` replaced). `arrays.cljc:28-182`.                          |     |       |\n   601\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   602\t\n   603\t**Table B: portable over the profile, no host arm (P).** Base64 (replaces\n   604\t`goog.crypt.base64`, `dart:convert`, the JVM codec; **a replacement, not code\n   605\tmotion**; oracle V `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc`, 3 deftests:\n   606\t`rfc-4648-round-trips`, `decode-is-total-and-strict`, `every-length-round-trips`);\n   607\tthe Jing CBOR writer (replaces Boring and the Dart `cbor` package on the\n   608\tcontent path only, OQ4; a replacement; oracle table D); hex; `chunks/split`,\n   609\t`chunks/absorb`.\n   610\t\n   611\t**Table C: runtime prerequisites (documented and verified by existing\n   612\tsuites; not profile entries; not a boundary).**\n   613\t\n   614\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   615\t| Prerequisite                     | Where, and the law a port must meet (V)                                                        | Slice   |\n   616\t+==================================+================================================================================================+=========+\n   617\t| `deftype` with per-host          | `values.cljc:39-119`: `Closure`/`Continuation` equal iff owner and payload equal; hash of      | H1 docs |\n   618\t| equality, hashing and printing   | `[:tag owner payload]`; print the marker text. `cbor.cljc:342-460`: `Float64` equal by bits    |         |\n   619\t|                                  | with NaN equal to NaN (`:365-367`); `Rational`, `Decimal` equal by fields; hashes at           |         |\n   620\t|                                  | `:372-444`.                                                                                    |         |\n   621\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   622\t| Atomic flag                      | `btree.cljc:87-119`: transient ownership token readable across threads.                        | none    |\n   623\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   624\t| Weak and soft references         | `btree.cljc:182-245`; default `:soft` on the JVM, `:strong` on JS and Dart (`:39-44`). A host  | none    |\n   625\t|                                  | without them declares `:strong`; correctness is unchanged, retention differs.                  |         |\n   626\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   627\t| `locking`, atoms, volatiles      | Five `locking` sites (§3.1); single-owner discipline elsewhere.                                | none    |\n   628\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   629\t| Host promise type                | `btree/storage.cljc:218-227`: deferred (§9.1).                                                 | defer   |\n   630\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   631\t| Dialect syntax                   | §3.3.                                                                                          | H0      |\n   632\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   633\t\n   634\tLayering: `dao.host.*` requires nothing in the repo; `dao` never requires\n   635\t`yin`. Consumers after H2: `dao.jing`, `dao.jing.cbor`, `yin.vm.integer`,\n   636\t`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.values`, `yin.vm.engine`, `yin.vm`, `yin.vm.debruijn`,\n   637\t`yin.vm.debruijn-code`, `dao.stream.chunks`, `dao.jing.dht`, `yin.vm.linker`,\n   638\t`yin.vm.linker.sign`, `dao.stream.datagram`, `dao.stream.base64`, and the\n   639\tthree Python integer tests.\n   640\t\n   641\t### 4.3 Oracle coverage matrix (table D)\n   642\t\n   643\tEntry to exact file and case. V = the case exists today and exercises the\n   644\tbehaviour through its present namespace; P = proposed, written in the slice\n   645\tnamed. After H1 every V case is additionally run against `dao.host.*`\n   646\tdirectly by `dao.host.conformance-test` (P), which requires the new\n   647\tnamespaces and re-asserts each row below through them (review A6).\n   648\t\n   649\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   650\t| Entries                         | File and case                                                                                           | V/P |\n   651\t+=================================+=========================================================================================================+=====+\n   652\t| integer: carriers, promote,     | `test/yin/vm/integer_test.cljc` (25 deftests): `carrier-boundary-test`, `compare-test`,                 | V   |\n   653\t| demote, add, sub, mul, quot,    | `division-test`, `bits-test`, `pow-test`, `parse-format-test`, `digit-limit-test`, `bit-limit-test`,    |     |\n   654\t| rem, compare, bit ops, shifts,  | `fast-path-edge- test`, `fast-path-respects-the-bit-limit-test`, `integer?-test`,                       |     |\n   655\t| bit length, radix               | `kind-of-and-number?-test`; `integer_v3_fixtures.cljc` (data).                                          |     |\n   656\t|                                 | `test/yang/python/antlr/int_contract_test.cljc`: `integer-rows- recompute-on-this-host`,                |     |\n   657\t|                                 | `canonical-widths-at-the-boundaries`, `text-round-trips-through-the-module` against                     |     |\n   658\t|                                 | `test/resources/yang/python/int-contract-v1.txt` (CPython-generated).                                   |     |\n   659\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   660\t| integer: `parse-decimal`,       | `test/dao/jing/cbor_conformance_test.cljc`: `the-resource-bytes-are-the-frozen-bytes`, `produced-bytes- | V   |\n 