 (80 deftests) example cases (V, examples only); `dao.host.text-test`:  | V+P |\n   687\t|                                 | a pinned subset of Unicode 16.0 `NormalizationTest.txt` (every part-1 line plus the Hangul and          |     |\n   688\t|                                 | composition exclusion rows); written in H1.                                                             |     |\n   689\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   690\t| hash: `blake3-bytes`,           | `test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc` (15 deftests): `blake3-official-and-utf8-vector-       | V+P |\n   691\t| `sha256-bytes`                  | conformance`, `fixtures-load-and-agree-with-canonical-bytes`, `segment-matches-total-predicate-blake3-  |     |\n   692\t|                                 | and-sha256`; `test/resources/dao/jing/digest-table.edn`; `jing_test.cljc` (39 deftests) address cases.  |     |\n   693\t|                                 | P in H3: NIST SHA-256 short-message vectors in `dao.host.hash-test`.                                    |     |\n   694\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   695\t| sign: `keypair-from-seed`,      | `test/yin/vm/linker/sign_test.cljc` (4 deftests): `rfc-8032-vectors`, `canonical-envelope-vectors`,     | V   |\n   696\t| `sign`, `verify`                | `tampering-is-bad-proof`, `key-file-validation`; `sign_vectors.edn`.                                    |     |\n   697\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   698\t| arrays: all twelve              | `test/dao/data/btree_test.cljc`, `btree_transients_test.cljc`, `psset_fixtures.cljc` (V, through the    | V+P |\n   699\t|                                 | tree); P in H2: `asort` stability fixture (equal keys keep input order), `acopy` overlap cases, and     |     |\n   700\t|                                 | **no-partial-write** cases for `acopy` and `aset` with an invalid index or length on all three lanes    |     |\n   701\t|                                 | (the array is identical after the refusal; today JS and Dart can write first, `arrays.cljc:97-105`).    |     |\n   702\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   703\t| Jing CBOR writer (table B)      | `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json` with `cbor-v1.errata.md` preserved; `cbor_fixtures_test.cljc`    | V   |\n   704\t|                                 | (14 deftests), `cbor_conformance_test.cljc` (14): byte-identical production, `documented-skips-match-   |     |\n   705\t|                                 | the-errata-and-leave-no-case-unrun`; `cbor_test.cljc`; `jing_test.cljc`; `file_test.cljc` (17) replay.  |     |\n   706\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   707\t| base64 (table B)                | `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc` (3 deftests, named above).                                           | V   |\n   708\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   709\t\n   710\t### 4.4 The driver\n   711\t\n   712\tPer host, outside the core: the seam values of §4.1, clock readings as data,\n   713\tstdin/stdout, process exit, ambient facts as data. `yin.repl.main` is that\n   714\ttoday (V). Its deferred duties (entropy deposit, pump cadence) are §9's.\n   715\t\n   716\t### 4.5 Relation to the conformance kit and the wasm surface\n   717\t\n   718\t`yin.vm.engine.md` §E.5 presupposes a correct host value model. H1 supplies\n   719\t`dao.host.conformance-test` (table D through the new namespaces); E.5.2's\n   720\t\"R, owner, seal, profile and manifest addresses bit-identical\" is downstream\n   721\tof it. The stream-implementation suite is deferred (§9.4).\n   722\t\n   723\t## 5. What porting a host consists of (after H0-H4)\n   724\t\n   725\t1. Implement table A (76 functions) and meet table C for the dialect; green\n   726\t   `dao.host.conformance-test`. Hash and signature bind a library compiled\n   727\t   into the same instance.\n   728\t2. Load the adopted closure with a reader feature only where §3.3 syntax\n   729\t   requires it; the H0 gate proves zero source edits outside `dao.host.*`\n   730\t   and the §9 deferred files.\n   731\t3. The deferred seams (§9) remain per-host work until their design lands;\n   732\t   until then a port supplies them as today's hosts do, by reader arms in\n   733\t   the deferred files, which H0's allowlist permits.\n   734\t\n   735\t## 6. Verifiability\n   736\t\n   737\tByte-level oracles exist for every hot primitive (table D). H0's gate has\n   738\ttwo lists (files permitted non-exempt arms, §8.1; resolved effect calls\n   739\tpermitted) and two negative tests; it scans recursively and treats reading\n   740\tzero files as a failure distinct from zero matches, as does its library\n   741\tmode (§8.2) for the H2 and H3 host-library gates. Every H1-H4 acceptance is\n   742\tbyte-identical against a named corpus with errata preserved; the two\n   743\tbehaviour changes (§10) each have a direct test.\n   744\t\n   745\t## 7. Consequence for wasm\n   746\t\n   747\tPrimitives execute in-instance. The import module `dao.stream` has exactly\n   748\tthe seven names of `dao.stream.wasm.md:38-46` (V); a primitive import is a\n   749\tboundary crossing and a violation of §2.2 whatever its purity. The gate that\n   750\tasserts a binary's import list is part of the deferred conformance suite\n   751\t(§9.4); until then the rule is stated here and checked by review.\n   752\t\n   753\t## 8. Slices H0-H4 (commissionable)\n   754\t\n   755\tExpand, migrate, contract. Each slice lands alone under the quick tier on\n   756\tthree lanes with recorded test and assertion counts; \"unchanged\" means equal\n   757\tcounts plus any added test named. The slow tier runs once after H4.\n   758\t\n   759\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   760\t| Slice | Phase  | Change                                                                         | Falsifiable acceptance                                            |\n   761\t+=======+========+================================================================================+===================================================================+\n   762\t| H0    | freeze | No `src/` change. (a) `src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (over                | Gate passes on the current tree; the committed closure output     |\n   763\t|       |        | `clojure.tools.namespace` parsing) and its output                              | lists exactly 142/140/141 files (§3.1) and the slice report       |\n   764\t|       |        | `docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn`, each file tagged with | records agreement with an independent traversal; the gate fails   |\n   765\t|       |        | its §3.1 class; (b) the gate test `dao.host.gate-test` over the closure with   | on one injected `#?(:clj` in a file outside list 1 and on one     |\n   766\t|       |        | **list 1** (files permitted non-exempt host arms, §8.1) and **list 2**         | injected `(random-uuid)` outside list 2 (two negative tests), and |\n   767\t|       |        | (resolved effect calls permitted: the §3.2 sites, plus the callers of M        | fails distinctly when it reads zero files (scan failure is not    |\n   768\t|       |        | entries named in §2.4), exempting §3.3 patterns; the gate scans files          | zero matches). Counts recorded.                                   |\n   769\t|       |        | recursively and fails if it read none; (c) per-lane counts; (d) the corpus     |                                                                   |\n   770\t|       |        | hash set.                                                                      |                                                                   |\n   771\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   772\t| H1    | expand | Create `dao.host.integer`, `.float`, `.number`, `.bytes`, `.text` with today's | Green; counts unchanged plus the named new tests; the new tests   |\n   773\t|       |        | arms moved verbatim where the law is today's behaviour, and **with the new     | require and call `dao.host.*` directly; corpus bytes identical;   |\n   774\t|       |        | laws where it is not**: `utf8-encode` refuses an unpaired surrogate (today's   | the P-entry argument-immutability property test and the M-entry   |\n   775\t|       |        | helpers substitute: JVM `getBytes` emits `?`, `goog.crypt` and `dart:convert`  | prevalidation test pass on three lanes; `utf8-encode` direct      |\n   776\t|       |        | emit U+FFFD, `jing.cljc:66,69,71,132-135`, `sign.cljc:62-66`, R for the        | refusal test and `utf8-decode` strict tests pass. List 1 grows by |\n   777\t|       |        | library behaviour); `utf8-decode` is extracted from the already strict         | five files.                                                       |\n   778\t|       |        | `cbor.cljc:1240-1271` (V). The `Float64`/`Rational`/`Decimal` deftypes move    |                                                                   |\n   779\t|       |        | with their protocol blocks. Tests: `dao.host.conformance-test`,              