or.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\n   814\t|       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\n   815\t|       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\n   816\t|       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\n   817\t|       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\n   818\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   819\t\n   820\tDependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\n   821\t\n   822\t### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\n   823\t\n   824\tThe gate never promises \"no arms across `src/cljc`\", only \"no non-exempt\n   825\tarms outside list 1\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\n   826\tclosure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\n   827\tthe **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\n   828\tdifference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\n   829\tis today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\n   830\t(five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\n   831\tmarked as such in the table.\n   832\t\n   833\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   834\t| Category (reason)        