{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '40,100p' src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc; sed -n '130,162p' src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc; rg -n 'a/(aset|acopy|asort)|arrays/(aset|acopy|asort)' src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc; rg -n 'dao.data.arrays' src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc; sed -n '590,602p' docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md; sed -n '368,400p' .claude/worktrees/host-h0/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj; sed -n '1,70p' collab/1792517656000-reviewer-host-boundary-r5.qwen3.8-max.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n(defn big-carrier?\n  \"True when `x` is a host big-integer carrier: `clojure.lang.BigInt` or\n   `BigInteger` on the JVM, a `BigInt` on JS and Dart. On JS and Dart\n   such a value answers false to `number?`.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x BigInt)\n     :clj (or (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt x) (instance? BigInteger x))\n     :cljs (js-bigint? x)))\n\n\n(defn exact-integer?\n  \"True when `x` is an exact integer in any carrier the host has: a JVM\n   `long`, `int`, `short`, `byte`, `BigInt` or `BigInteger`; a JS\n   safe-integer `Number` other than `-0`, or a `BigInt`; a Dart `int` or\n   `BigInt`. A float with an integral value is not, except on JS, which\n   cannot tell `1.0` from `1`.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (or (dart/is? x int) (dart/is? x BigInt))\n     :clj (or (instance? Long x) (instance? Integer x) (instance? Short x)\n              (instance? Byte x) (instance? clojure.lang.BigInt x)\n              (instance? BigInteger x))\n     :cljs (or (js-bigint? x)\n               (and (number? x)\n                    (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)\n                    ;; -0 is the one zero whose reciprocal is negative\n                    (not (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1 x))))))))\n\n\n(defn safe-native?\n  \"True when `x` is a native carrier within +/-(2^53 - 1): a JVM `long`,\n   a Dart `int`, or exactly the `Number` arm of `exact-integer?` on JS.\n   Two such values add, subtract and compare natively without rounding\n   or wrapping on every host.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (and (dart/is? x int)\n                (<= -9007199254740991 x)\n                (<= x 9007199254740991))\n     :clj (and (instance? Long x)\n               (let [n (.longValue ^Long x)]\n                 (and (<= -9007199254740991 n) (<= n 9007199254740991))))\n     :cljs (and (number? x)\n                (js/Number.isSafeInteger x)\n                (not (and (zero? x) (neg? (/ 1 x)))))))\n\n\n(defn host-float?\n  \"True when `x` is a host binary64: a JVM `Double`, a Dart `double`, any\n   JS `Number`.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (dart/is? x double)\n     :clj (instance? Double x)\n     :cljs (number? x)))\n\n\n(defn nan-float?\n  \"True when host float `x` is a NaN.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (.-isNaN ^double x)\n     :clj (Double/isNaN (double x))\n     :cljs (js/isNaN x)))\n     :cljs (.charCodeAt s i)))\n\n\n(defn- high-surrogate?\n  [u]\n  (<= 0xD800 u 0xDBFF))\n\n\n(defn- low-surrogate?\n  [u]\n  (<= 0xDC00 u 0xDFFF))\n\n\n(defn- code-points\n  \"The code points of string `s`: a surrogate pair decodes to one code\n   point, an unpaired surrogate is its own.\"\n  [s]\n  (let [n (unit-count s)]\n    (loop [i 0\n           out (transient [])]\n      (if (< i n)\n        (let [u (code-unit s i)\n              v (when (< (inc i) n) (code-unit s (inc i)))]\n          (if (and (high-surrogate? u) v (low-surrogate? v))\n            (recur (+ i 2)\n                   (conj! out (+ 0x10000\n                                 (* (- u 0xD800) 0x400)\n                                 (- v 0xDC00))))\n            (recur (inc i) (conj! out u))))\n        (persistent! out)))))\n\n\n(defn- units->string\n19:            [dao.data.arrays :as arr]))\n255:   locals/return (§3.2 note in dao.data.arrays): the JFR profiling record\n|                    | `sign.cljc:62-66`.                                                                                   |     |       |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n| `dao.host.hash`    | P: `blake3-bytes`, `sha256-bytes` (`jing.cljc:59-135`; the string forms become portable over         | 2   | H3    |\n|                    | `text`).                                                                                             |     |       |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n| `dao.host.sign`    | P: `keypair-from-seed` (`sign.cljc:75-104`, seed replay), `sign`, `verify`. `generate` (fresh        | 3   | H3    |\n|                    | entropy, `:114-124`) stays in `yin.vm.linker.sign` until the deferred design moves it.               |     |       |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n| `dao.data.arrays`  | In place (OQ2). P: `anew` (fresh), `aget`, `alength`, `aclone` (fresh), `asub` (fresh), `aconcat`    | 12  | H2    |\n| (member by         | (fresh), `ainsert-at` (fresh), `aremove-at` (fresh), `from-coll` (fresh); M: `aset`, `acopy`         |     |       |\n| reference)         | (memmove), `asort` (stable; `parallelSort` replaced). `arrays.cljc:28-182`.                          |     |       |\n+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n\n\n\n(defn effect-calls\n  \"[[kind line] ...] for the resolved effect calls in forms.\"\n  [forms]\n  (let [{:keys [aliases refers shadowed]} (file-scope forms)\n        acc (atom [])\n        hit! (fn [kind sym] (swap! acc conj [kind (line-of sym)]))\n        resolve-m (fn [sym]\n                    (if-let [q (namespace sym)]\n                      (get aliases (symbol q) (symbol q))\n                      (get refers sym)))]\n    (letfn [(walk\n              [form bound]\n              (cond\n                (symbol? form)\n                (when-not (and (nil? (namespace form)) (bound form))\n                  (if-let [k (effect-kind form (not (shadowed form)))]\n                    (hit! k form)\n                    (when (and (m-entry-nss (resolve-m form)) (m-entry-names (name form)))\n                      (hit! :m-entry form))))\n\n                (seq? form)\n                (let [h (head form)]\n                  (cond\n                    (#{'quote 'comment 'ns} h) nil\n                    (let-heads h) (walk-let (second form) (nnext form) bound)\n                    (= 'letfn h) (let [fns (second form)\n                                       b (into bound (map first fns))]\n                                   (doseq [f fns] (walk-fn (rest f) b))\n                                   (walk-all (nnext form) b))\n                    (fn-heads h) (walk-fn (rest form) bound)\n                    (= 'catch h) (walk-all (drop 3 form) (conj bound (nth form 2 nil)))\nBoth §8.3 false-positive cites verified: `dao/data.cljc:54` is a docstring (\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\"), `lowering.cljc:587` is `:rgba8unorm` in a keyword literal. All checks complete.\n\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-20 17:34:16 GMT\nCoding-Agent: cmd | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Role: Reviewer (read-only)\nDocument: docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (r5, 1,179 lines)\n\n**Verdict: APPLIED WITH DEFECTS** (three Low; none invalidate M1-M4)\n\n**Disposition M1-M4**\n- **M1: APPLIED.** §2.4 (lines 226-244) splits ownership transfer from freezing publication; \"Returning fresh storage is not publication\" (line 235-236); caller mutation right (`set!`/`copy!`/`aset`/`acopy`/`asort`) preserved. Obligations (i)-(iv) (lines 245-260) intact and match §14's reference.\n- **M2: APPLIED.** §8.3 (lines 804-822): reader-level scan of closure-tagged files, comments/strings/docstrings excluded by construction, both false-positive sites named (verified above), codec-track files unscanned but retained on list 1, scan err